 call this function from the body of an asynchronous function,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the unsafe task handle passed to the closure is always non-","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"because an asynchronous function always runs in the context of a task.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"However, if you call this function from the body of a synchronous function,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and that function isn’t executing in the context of any task,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the unsafe task handle is ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t store an unsafe task reference","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for use outside this method’s closure.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Storing an unsafe reference doesn’t affect the task’s actual life cycle,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and the behavior of accessing an unsafe task reference","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"outside of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"withUnsafeCurrentTask(body:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method’s closure isn’t defined.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"There’s no safe way to retrieve a reference to the current task","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and save it for long-term use.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"To query the current task without saving a reference to it,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use properties like ","type":"text"},{"code":"currentPriority","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"If you need to store a reference to a task,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"create an unstructured task using ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task.detache